#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
A convincing fake shell for the web01 honeypot.

Nothing here ever executes attacker input. Commands are implemented in Python
against an in-memory virtual filesystem, so the shell can be wrong but never
dangerous.

The design goal is surviving fingerprinting. Bots routinely check:
  - exact error strings ("No such file or directory" vs "command not found")
  - whether a file can be written, chmod'ed, executed and removed
  - $(...) substitution, || fallback chains, pipes, redirection
so all of those behave the way bash does.
"""

