# The host namespace inode numbers, which are the same fixed set on every
# Linux since 3.8. /proc/<pid>/ns/ was an empty directory while `lsns`
# printed three of these out of a literal, so the command and the files it
# reads disagreed about whether this box has namespaces at all -- and
# comparing /proc/self/ns/mnt with /proc/1/ns/mnt is how every container
# check ever written asks whether it is boxed in.
# Every mount on the box, in the order the kernel made them. This was nine
# lines of /proc/mounts and a separate six-row table inside df, and neither
# knew about the pseudo-filesystems a real trixie has: no cgroup2, on a box
# whose own MEMORY_PRESSURE_WATCH paths live under /sys/fs/cgroup, and no
# tmpfs on /tmp, which trixie mounts by default and which decides whether a
# dropper's payload survives a reboot. 9 mounts against the guest's 29.
# (source, target, fstype, options, superopts, dev)
